# Abyss Racer — Versus round 2 feedback (from Konstantin after playing with a friend)

You built the versus mode (see VERSUS.md, README.md, STATUS.md, docs/versus.js, docs/contacts.js). Four changes requested. Keep everything else intact; keep all test suites green and extend them for each change.

## 1. Make it easier to pass the other player (MUST)
Right now rover–rover contacts block side-by-side overtaking: the trailing rover just pushes against the leader and can't get past. Change contacts so that **overtaking is easy and physical interaction is still fun**:
- When both rovers are (roughly) on the ground and side-by-side (vertical centre offset < ~0.6 rover height), do NOT resolve wheel/chassis contacts between them at all — they pass through each other like ghosts. Draw the rover that is farther back in that viewport at ~55% opacity while they overlap so it reads as "behind".
- Keep contacts when one rover is clearly above the other (landing on someone, driving off their roof, dome-from-above crush) — that's the fun part. Use hysteresis so the contact mode doesn't flicker mid-overlap (e.g. once ghosting starts it persists until they're horizontally separated by > 1.2 rover lengths).
- Strengthen the catch-up current: +12% → +25% top speed and +15% torque when more than 60 m behind, fading out by 20 m. Show the icon as now.
- Add a slipstream: within 8–40 m directly behind the leader on the ground, +10% top speed ("SLIPSTREAM" tag).

## 2. Torpedo must actually kill (MUST)
A torpedo hit currently only shoves/spins the victim. Change: a torpedo hit on an unshielded player is an instant crash ("Torpedoed!") → the normal 2.5 s respawn cycle, counts as a crash, credited as an item landed. Keep the ballast-jump dodge (torpedo passes under an airborne rover) and the shield block. Add a proper explosion: bubble burst + flash + screen shake in both viewports, and a distinct sound. Make torpedoes a bit faster than the top speed of the fastest vehicle at level 5 so they can't be outrun forever, but keep the max 12 s life.

## 3. Respawn when out of oxygen (MUST)
Running out of oxygen currently eliminates a player for the round. Change:
- **Race and Pearl Rush**: at 0 oxygen the player "blacks out": 4 s respawn countdown ("OUT OF AIR · RESPAWN 4.0 s") at their position, then respawn with 60% oxygen. Counts in a separate "blackouts" stat shown on results. No elimination in these modes.
- **Last Sub Standing**: give each player 3 lives (shown as small O₂ tank icons in the HUD). Out of oxygen costs a life and triggers the same 4 s respawn with 60% oxygen; losing the last life eliminates. Last player with a life wins; if both lose their last life in the same step, the one with more distance wins. Update the mode description on the setup screen.

## 4. Resolution is really low (MUST — Konstantin noticed it immediately on a Retina Mac)
The "adaptive ocean resolution" (dropping to 0.5 px per CSS px on slow frames) and the versus DPR cap of 1.5 make the game look blurry. Remove the automatic downscaling entirely. Requirements:
- Render at `min(window.devicePixelRatio, 2)` in both solo and versus, always. Never below 1.
- Instead, make rendering cheap enough: profile the versus frame with two viewports and optimise (cache the seabed fill/sand-edge path per terrain chunk in offscreen canvases keyed by chunk+zoom bucket, cache decorations per chunk, cap ambient particles per viewport, avoid per-frame gradient creation, avoid shadowBlur, cull everything outside each viewport with a margin, avoid re-drawing static HUD text every frame). Target: 60 fps at 1440×900 @2x on a 2019 MacBook Pro in versus; measure what you can in headless and report rendered fps at 1440×900 @2x before/after.
- Add a **Graphics** setting (Title → How to play panel or the pause menu, and versus setup): "Crisp (default) / Performance". Performance = 1.0 px per CSS px and fewer particles. Persist it in the save (settings.graphics). Default is Crisp. No automatic switching.
- Verify in a headless screenshot at deviceScaleFactor 2 that `canvas.width === Math.round(clientWidth * 2)` for the game canvas in versus and solo, and that text/lines are sharp.

## Tests / verification
- Extend tests/versus.test.cjs (or add versus2.test.cjs): (a) overtaking: place P2 15 px behind P1 on flat ground, both grounded, P2 at 380 px/s and P1 at 200 px/s → P2 must be ahead by > 60 px within 2 s with no crash; (b) landing crush still works: place P1 60 px above P2 and let it fall → contact resolves (bounce or crush); (c) torpedo hit → victim.crashed === 'Torpedoed!' and respawn within 3 s; shield blocks it; airborne dodge passes; (d) oxygen 0 in Race → respawn within ~4.5 s with 60% oxygen, blackouts stat = 1; Last Sub Standing → lives 3→2 and respawn; last life → eliminated; (e) canvas backing size equals CSS size × min(dpr,2) at dpr 2 for solo and versus; (f) all existing suites still pass. Provide debug hooks (`?debug=1`): `AR.debug.setOxygen(i, value)`, `AR.debug.placePlayer(i, {x, y, vx})` (exists), `AR.debug.fireTorpedo(i)` if needed.
