70. Never label a number merely "judgment"/"team judgment" — always state the reasoning that makes the chosen value most plausible (anchors, constraints, why this end of the range) (KP 2026-07-09).
71. Sheet design: Assumptions tab = boring parameters only (FX, constants); substantive inputs live on the working tab inside the table with reasoning adjacent; derivations are visible rows, not separate blocks; no duplication (KP 2026-07-09).
