96. Fade-bar figures: no p10/p90 tick lines, no median lines, no zoom side-panels — density fade + printed median only (KP 2026-08-11, holy-grail EOY-2026 forecast figure).
71. **Poll Sol/codex agents every ~5 min.** Completion notifications for detached codex runs often never arrive; while any Sol/codex agent works, wake every ~5 minutes and check its output files until deliverables land. (KP 2026-08-12)
72. **Pipeline-database forecasts are valid p50s.** Never collapse a national/annual estimate to named construction-verified projects when a full-coverage pipeline forecast (EUDCA, DC Byte, KF) exists — those discount delays already; named ledgers are floors. Same-edition differencing only. (KP 2026-08-13)
73. **Parallelize disjoint Sheet edits.** Multiple agents editing explicit non-overlapping cells/ranges should write concurrently; do not put the whole workbook or full agent turns behind one lock. Serialize only overlaps, structural/broad-formatting changes, and final reconciliation. Re-read stable labels, use narrow writes, and run one workbook-wide QA afterward. This session was slow because safe regional edits were unnecessarily queued; the actual failures were nested locking, command syntax, and a structural circular reference—not concurrent different-cell edits. → [feedback_parallel_sheet_edits.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_parallel_sheet_edits.md) (KP 2026-08-13)
74. **Parallelize at the smallest independent unit.** For multi-row research, default to one agent per independent row/region/company/source. If in-process slots are insufficient, use monitored external Sol sessions for overflow. Keep blind estimates isolated, give each agent a unique output path, then aggregate and red-team after all finish. → [feedback_aggressive_parallel_agent_granularity.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_aggressive_parallel_agent_granularity.md) (KP 2026-08-14)
75. **Use deterministic completion detection for parallel agents.** Every detached batch needs per-agent `DONE` markers, a monitored parent process that waits and validates all workers, and an independent watcher that reports `N/N` completion or failures. Never rely only on agents messaging back; poll Sol/Codex jobs about every five minutes. → [feedback_parallel_completion_detection.md](projects/-home-ubuntu/memory/feedback_parallel_completion_detection.md) (KP 2026-08-14)
77. Wind down idle infrastructure (keepalive, watchers, monitors) after ~4h of KP inactivity once work is delivered — save state to disk first, note they can be rearmed on request; don't stand watch for days (2026-08-17)
