from pathlib import Path
p=Path('README.md'); s=p.read_text()
s=s.replace('First to 500, 1,000, or 2,000 m wins. If both run out of oxygen, the furthest distance wins.', 'First to 500, 1,000, or 2,000 m wins. Empty oxygen causes a 4-second blackout, then a respawn at the same position with 60% air; nobody is eliminated.')
s=s.replace('No distance target. Oxygen drains 1.5× faster, with tanks at one-third the usual frequency. The last player with oxygen wins.', 'Three lives, shown as O₂ tank icons. Oxygen drains 1.5× faster, with tanks at one-third the usual frequency. Empty oxygen costs a life: respawn after 4 seconds with 60% air, or eliminate on the final life. The last player with a life wins; simultaneous final losses compare distance.')
s=s.replace('Most pearls after 90 seconds wins. Pickups are shared: collecting one removes it for both players. An empty tank stops pickups and scoring for that player, but they can keep driving and use a held item; ballast is unavailable. If both tanks are empty, compare the current pearl scores immediately.', 'Most pearls after 90 seconds wins. Pickups are shared: collecting one removes it for both players. Empty oxygen causes the same 4-second blackout and 60% air respawn. Scoring resumes afterward; the timer continues through blackouts.')
s=s.replace('distances, crashes, items used, and pearls for 3 seconds', 'distances, crashes, blackouts, items used, and pearls for 3 seconds').replace('best distance, items landed, crashes, and torpedoes dodged', 'best distance, items landed, crashes, blackouts, and torpedoes dodged')
s=s.replace('Both rovers occupy the same physics world and can ram, shove, and land on each other.', 'Both rovers occupy the same physics world. Grounded side-by-side overlaps ghost through one another so overtaking stays easy; the trailing rover draws at 55% opacity during overlap. Ghosting persists until horizontal separation exceeds 1.2 rover lengths. Landings from above still resolve physically, including driving off a roof and dome crushes.')
s=s.replace('An empty tank eliminates a player for the round, with the Pearl Rush exception above. A player more than 80 m behind receives a **catch-up current**: +12% top speed until the gap closes to 30 m.', 'Empty air causes **OUT OF AIR · RESPAWN 4.0 s**, tracked as a separate **blackouts** statistic. Only the final Last Sub Standing life eliminates. A player at least 60 m behind receives a **catch-up current**: +25% top speed and +15% torque, fading linearly to zero by 20 m. Being 8–40 m directly behind the opponent, with both rovers near the ground, grants another +10% top speed and a **SLIPSTREAM** tag.')
s=s.replace('A hit adds a strong shove and spin. A shield blocks it; a ballast jump can dodge it.', 'An unshielded hit instantly crashes the victim (**Torpedoed"'!**), counts as an item landed and a crash, and starts the normal 2.5-second respawn. A bubble explosion, flash, shake in both viewports, and distinct sound mark the hit. Speed is 1,811 px/s, above even a fully boosted level-5 bike. A shield blocks it; a ballast jump can dodge it.'"')
s=s.replace('An oxygen-empty user cannot gain points.', 'A blacked-out user cannot use items until respawning.')
s=s.replace('Versus caches terrain strips, decorative plants, rigid hull art, and lighting textures while culling each viewport independently. On sustained slow frames, the ocean backing buffer reduces its pixel density; the HUD, player tags, and gap labels stay at native resolution. Solo and setup restore the original native canvas resolution.', '**Graphics** is available in **Title → How to play** and **Versus setup**. **Crisp (default)** always uses "'`max(1, min(devicePixelRatio, 2))` backing pixels per CSS pixel in solo and versus. **Performance** explicitly uses 1× and fewer particles. The choice persists in `settings.graphics`; there is no automatic switching. Terrain fill/sand edges and background decorations are cached by chunk and zoom bucket; rigid hulls, wheels, pickups, labels, and gradients use bounded sprite caches. Each viewport culls independently and caps particles. HUD text updates only when its value changes.'"')
s=s.replace('node tests/versus.test.cjs\\n"'```'"', 'node tests/versus.test.cjs\\nnode tests/graphics.test.cjs\\nnode tests/render-benchmark.cjs after-crisp\\n"'```'"')
a=s.index('"'`tests/contacts.test.cjs` covers'"'); b=s.index('\\n\\nFor local debugging',a)
s=s[:a]+'''"'`tests/contacts.test.cjs` checks all 25 vehicle pairings ghosting on the ground, the specified 380-versus-200 px/s pass within 2 seconds, overlap hysteresis, 60 px landings, dome crushes, and resting stability. `tests/versus-logic.test.cjs` covers catch-up/slipstream, shared pickups and finish ordering, lethal torpedoes with shield/dodge defenses, blackouts in Race/Pearl Rush, three survival lives and simultaneous final-life distance decisions, respawn costs, and shields. `tests/versus-save-audio.test.cjs` covers tally/save isolation and all item/explosion audio cues. `tests/versus.test.cjs` exercises keyboard play, items, modes, respawns, results, and persistence in Chromium. `tests/graphics.test.cjs` verifies backing sizes in both modes at DPR 2, the DPR floor/cap, manual Graphics persistence, and immunity to slow-frame downscaling, and captures `/tmp/abyss-fix2-solo.png` and `/tmp/abyss-fix2-versus.png` at 1440×900 @2×. These additions preserve the solo suites.

`tests/render-benchmark.cjs` measures rendered animation frames over eight seconds after three seconds of warm-up, profiling renderer methods while both cameras follow a repeatable trajectory. Run it alone: concurrent Chromium tests compete for raster time. Its `AR.debug` fixture controls positions; simulation tick counters are never reported as rendered fps. JSON output goes to `/tmp/abyss-fix2-fps-<label>.json`.'"''' +s[b:]
s=s.replace('"'`crashPlayer(playerIndex)`, and `advance(seconds)`'"', '"'`crashPlayer(playerIndex)`, `setOxygen(playerIndex, value)`, `fireTorpedo(playerIndex)`, and `advance(seconds)`'"')
a=s.index('Versus round 2 validation:'); b=s.index('\\n\\nChrome/Chromium',a)
s=s[:a]+'''Versus feedback fixes: gameplay regression suites currently pass (9 contact checks, 18 controller checks, save/audio checks); full browser/graphics validation is in progress. Final evidence and the equal-resolution before/after measurements are recorded in "'`FIX2_DONE.txt`. A 2019 MacBook Pro is unavailable in this environment, so its 60 fps target cannot be verified here.'"''' +s[b:]
p.write_text(s)
p=Path('tests/CONTRACT.md'); s=p.read_text().replace(\"settings:{muted:false,headlight:'aqua',trail:'bubbles'}\", \"settings:{muted:false,headlight:'aqua',trail:'bubbles',graphics:'crisp'}\")
s=s.replace('1. "'`race`: first to target distance wins. If both cross during the same fixed step, compare interpolated crossing fractions; equal crossing fractions tie. If both oxygen reserves empty before the target, furthest distance wins; equal distances tie.'"', '1. "'`race`: first to target distance wins. If both cross during the same fixed step, compare interpolated crossing fractions; equal crossing fractions tie. Empty oxygen causes a blackout rather than ending the round.'"')
s=s.replace('One remaining reserve wins; simultaneously empty reserves tie.', 'Each player starts with three lives. Empty oxygen costs one life; the final loss eliminates. The last player with a life wins; simultaneous final losses compare distance, tying only if distance is also equal.')
s=s.replace('compare pearls after 90 seconds, or immediately if both reserves are empty. Equal pearls tie. An exhausted player remains able to drive, collide, and use a held item, but cannot collect pickups, gain pearls, or use ballast for the rest of the round.', 'compare pearls after 90 seconds. Equal pearls tie. Empty oxygen causes a blackout; scoring resumes after respawn.')
s=s.replace('activate +12% top speed beyond an 80 m deficit, retain until within 30 m.', 'linearly fade +25% top speed and +15% torque from full strength at 60 m to zero at 20 m. Grounded trailing rovers 8–40 m behind get +10% slipstream speed.')
s=s.replace(\"Oxygen depletion eliminates a player for the round, except for Pearl Rush's continued-driving rule.\", \"Oxygen depletion increments "'`blackouts`, freezes the rover at its position for 4 seconds, and respawns with 60% oxygen and spawn protection. Only the final survival life eliminates. If a crash oxygen deduction reaches zero, a blackout begins exactly once.")
s=s.replace('"'maximum 12 s; shove/spin on hit', 'maximum 12 s; instant Torpedoed"'! crash on unshielded hit'"')
s=s.replace('"'`out`, `catchup`, `effects`'"', '"'`out`, `catchup`, `slipstream`, `blackouts`, `lives`, `respawnKind`, `effects`'"')
s=s.replace('| "'`advance(seconds)`'"', '| "'`setOxygen(playerIndex, value)` | Set finite oxygen, clamped to the tank capacity; next fixed step applies depletion. |'"\\n| "'`fireTorpedo(playerIndex)` | Grant and launch a torpedo through normal item logic while RUNNING. |'"\\n| "'`advance(seconds)`'"')
s+='''\\nFIX2 rendering: "'`.setGraphics('"'crisp'|'performance')"'` applies a fixed density (Crisp: clamp DPR to [1,2]; Performance:1). `scene.explosions` contains `{x,y,life,maxLife}`, `scene.shake` is normalized 0..1 in versus, and `scene.flash` is remaining flash seconds. Rover `.ghosting` indicates a hysteretic ground overlap; render the rear rover at .55 only while visually overlapping. Both views display the same explosion, shake, and flash. Chunk caches use terrain identity, chunk, and upward-rounded quarter-zoom buckets. Static HUD DOM and cached name tags avoid unchanged text repaints. `tests/graphics.test.cjs` checks sizes/settings; `tests/render-benchmark.cjs` measures actual frame timestamps.'"\\n'''
p.write_text(s)
