codex
The final cache change raised the equal-resolution headless result to **7.4 fps**, from **4.3 fps** before. I also adjusted torpedoes to **959 px/s**, 10% above the fastest level-5 base speed, so the ballast dodge retains a reasonable timing window. Final checks now include the rear rover’s 55% opacity and screenshots of the explosion and blackout countdown.
exec
/bin/bash -lc "python3 - <<'PY'
from pathlib import Path
p=Path('tests/graphics.test.cjs'); s=p.read_text(); s=s.replace(\"      for (let i = 0; i < 600; i++) r.updateResolution(false, .05, { y: 0 });\\n      return { width: c.width, dpr: r.dpr };\", \"      for (const versus of [false, true]) for (let i = 0; i < 600; i++) r.updateResolution(versus, .05, { y: 0 });\\n      const size = { width: c.width, dpr: r.dpr }; r.showAwarenessLayer(false); r.awarenessCanvas.remove();\\n      let count = 0; const ellipse = r.ctx.ellipse.bind(r.ctx); r.ctx.ellipse = (...args) => { count++; return ellipse(...args); };\\n      r.versusView = true; r.ambient(r.ctx, { id: 'reef' }); const crispParticles = count; count = 0;\\n      r.graphics = 'performance'; r.ambient(r.ctx, { id: 'reef' });\\n      return { ...size, crispParticles, performanceParticles: count };\")
s=s.replace('assert.equal(slow.dpr, 2); await backing(2);', \"assert.equal(slow.dpr, 2); assert(slow.performanceParticles < slow.crispParticles, 'Performance reduces particles'); await backing(2);\")
p.write_text(s)
p=Path('README.md'); s=p.read_text().replace('Speed is 1,811 px/s, above even a fully boosted level-5 bike.', 'Speed is 959 px/s, 10% above the fastest level-5 base speed; the temporary Turbo Current lasts 3 seconds.')
p.write_text(s)
