ABYSS RACER — VERSUS FEEDBACK FIXES (FIX2)
2026-09-12

Implemented
1. Ground overtaking skips all rover–rover resolution when centres are within 0.6 rover height and both are near the ground. Ghosting persists until separation exceeds 1.2 rover lengths. The rear rover draws at 55% during overlap, with separated player tags. Above-rover landings, roof contacts and dome crushes retain physical impulses. The exact 15px / 380-versus-200px/s flat-ground test passes by 302.8px within2s. Catch-up adds25% top speed and15% torque at60m, fading linearly to zero at20m; ground slipstream adds10% within8–40m.
2. Unshielded torpedoes instantly set crashed='Torpedoed"'!'"', increment crashes/items landed once and trigger the normal2.5s respawn. Bubble burst, flash and shake appear in both viewports; torpedoHit has a distinct synth cue. Shield and ballast dodge remain effective. Speed959px/s = ceil(871px/s fastest level5 base speed ×1.10); maximum life12s. Temporary Turbo lasts3s.
3. Race/Pearl Rush empty oxygen causes a4s blackout at the same X, restoring60% oxygen and spawn protection; no elimination. Blackouts have a separate results stat. Last Sub Standing starts with3 lives and tank HUD icons; empty oxygen costs a life, final loss eliminates, simultaneous final losses compare distance. Crash oxygen costs and siphon depletion also trigger blackouts correctly. An oxygen pickup on the depletion step can rescue the rover without a spurious crash.
4. Removed automatic resolution changes and versus1.5x cap. Crisp defaults to clamp(devicePixelRatio,1,2) in both modes. Manual Performance uses1x and fewer particles, persists as settings.graphics and is available in Title→How to play and versus setup. Invalid/legacy values default to Crisp. Full seabed fill/sand-edge tiles and background decorations cache by terrain/chunk/quarter-zoom bucket. Foreground decorations retain individual cached art so they can clear the rover. Wheels/chassis/pickups/labels and gradients cache as immutable ImageBitmaps where available, with canvas fallback and bounded resource release. All world layers cull per viewport; particles are capped; no shadowBlur; HUD text updates only when changed.

Debug hooks (only ?debug=1)
AR.debug.setOxygen(i,value), placePlayer(i,{x,y,vx,...}), fireTorpedo(i), giveItem(i,id), crashPlayer(i), advance(seconds). Indices0/1. AR.inspect includes blackouts,lives,ghosting,slipstream,respawnKind and explosion state.

Rendered performance — same1440×900 CSS viewport at deviceScaleFactor2
Host:4-core ARM Neoverse-N1 Linux server. Chromium headless shell1243, --disable-gpu; software rendering, not a2019 MacBook Pro. Baseline renderer from97fcb38. tests/render-benchmark.cjs runs both production cameras/HUDs along the same scripted trajectory, warms3s, then measures about8s of actual rAF timestamps. Debug simulation ticks are not counted as rendered frames. Browser benchmarks ran serially.
- BEFORE, legacy adaptive:91frames/7.9997s =11.38fps; backing had fallen to1296×810 (0.9x). This is lower image quality and is not the equal-resolution comparison.
- BEFORE, old renderer forced to2x:34frames/7.8497s =4.33fps; backing2880×1800; p95 frame233.4ms.
- AFTER, Crisp2x:59frames/8.0164s =7.36fps; backing2880×1800; p95 frame150ms. Equal-resolution improvement69.9%.
- AFTER, manual Performance1x:207frames/8.0164s =25.82fps; backing1440×900; p95 frame50ms.
Profile: first canvas-cache iteration submitted about97.6ms/frame at2x. Immutable snapshots reduced that to43.4ms; decorations27.4ms, terrain6.4ms and rover drawing8.9ms dominate this software path. The old renderer deferred more raster work (2.1ms submission despite4.33fps), so submission duration alone is not a useful before/after FPS comparison.
Raw evidence: /tmp/abyss-fix2-fps-before-adaptive.json, before-crisp.json, after-bitmap.json, after-performance.json (all with the same /tmp/abyss-fix2-fps- prefix).

