/bin/bash -lc "python3 - <<'PY'
from pathlib import Path
p=Path('README.md'); s=p.read_text(); a=s.index('Versus feedback fixes:'); b=s.index('\\n\\nChrome/Chromium',a)
s=s[:a]+'''Versus feedback fixes (FIX2): **all nine regression suites pass**, including 27 physics checks, 13 progression/audio checks, 9 contact checks, 19 versus controller checks, save/audio, full versus integration, graphics, and unchanged solo browser/edge suites. The specified ground pass reached a 302.8 px lead within 2 seconds. Solo and versus both verify **2880×1800 backing at 1440×900 CSS / DPR 2**; their screenshots were personally inspected and are sharp and unclipped. Graphics tests also verify overlap alpha, both modes resisting slow-frame downscaling, reduced Performance particles, and settings persistence. Browser suites report zero application errors/warnings or external requests.

At equal **1440×900 @2×**, the repeatable software Chromium benchmark improved from **4.33 to 7.36 rendered fps**. Manual Performance measured **25.82 fps at 1×**. The old adaptive renderer measured 11.38 fps while dropping to 0.9×; that is not an equal-quality comparison. This ARM64 server did **not** reach 60 fps. A 2019 MacBook Pro is unavailable, so the requested hardware target remains unverified. Raw timings, methodology, screenshots, and limitations are recorded in "'`FIX2_DONE.txt`.'"''' +s[b:]
p.write_text(s)
p=Path('STATUS.md'); s=p.read_text().replace('FIX2 implementation complete; final browser, screenshot, and rendering checks in progress.', 'FIX2 implemented and all nine regression suites pass. Retina backing sizes and screenshots verified; the target MacBook Pro frame rate remains unverified.')
a=s.index('## Versus feedback fixes (FIX2)')
s=s[:a]+'''## Versus feedback fixes (FIX2) — complete, with performance limitation

1. Ground passes ghost with hysteresis; the rear rover draws at 55% opacity. Above-rover landings and crushes stay physical. Catch-up adds up to 25% speed / 15% torque, fading between 60 and 20 m; grounded slipstream adds 10% within 8–40 m.
2. Torpedoes travel at 959 px/s and instantly cause “Torpedoed"'!” with the normal 2.5-second respawn, crash/item credit, a bubble explosion, shared flash/shake, and a distinct cue. Shields and an actual keyboard ballast dodge pass regression checks.
3. Race/Pearl Rush empty oxygen causes a 4-second blackout and 60% oxygen respawn. Blackouts are separate results statistics. Survival has three lives, tank HUD icons, and distance adjudication for simultaneous final losses. Crash oxygen penalties, siphon depletion, and same-step oxygen pickup rescue are covered.
4. Crisp uses fixed DPR clamped to [1,2] in both modes. Manual Performance uses 1× and fewer particles; settings.graphics persists via the title help panel and versus setup. No automatic downscaling remains. Terrain/decorations cache by chunk and zoom bucket; rigid art, pickups, labels and gradients use bounded immutable sprite caches with canvas fallback. Per-viewport culling, particle caps, and unchanged-text guards reduce drawing work.

Final validation: physics 27/27; progression/audio 13/13; contacts 9/9 (all 25 vehicle pairs, specified pass, hysteresis, 60 px landing); versus logic 19/19; versus save/audio; full versus Chromium integration; graphics; unchanged solo desktop/mobile integration and edge suites. All pass. JS/CJS syntax and git diff whitespace checks pass. Browser suites have zero application errors/warnings or external requests. The passing final versus suite uses 959 px/s torpedoes and the final immutable renderer caches.

Both 1440×900 CSS game canvases have exactly 2880×1800 backing at DPR 2. Final solo/versus screenshots personally inspected: sharp text, rover outlines and terrain edges, no clipped HUDs. Additional overtake/explosion/blackout captures inspected; rear opacity is also asserted from the real Canvas context. Survival tank and compact HUD screenshots inspected.

| Same headless workload, requested viewport 1440×900 @2× | Actual backing density | Rendered fps |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Old adaptive renderer | 0.9× at sample end | 11.38 |
| Old renderer forced to Crisp resolution | 2× | 4.33 |
| Final Crisp | 2× | 7.36 |
| Final explicit Performance | 1× | 25.82 |

Equal-resolution improvement: 69.9%. Measurements use actual rAF timestamps after warm-up, with both cameras/HUDs following a repeatable trajectory, on a 4-core ARM Neoverse-N1 server with GPU disabled. **60 fps was not achieved here; a 2019 MacBook Pro is unavailable, so its target frame rate is unverified.** Actual Safari/Firefox and human sound balance remain untested. Benchmark browsers ran serially.

Evidence: `FIX2_DONE.txt`, `/tmp/abyss-fix2-fps-*.json`, `/tmp/abyss-fix2-graphics.json`, `/tmp/abyss-fix2-{solo,versus,overtake,explosion,blackout}.png`, `/tmp/abyss-fix2-gameplay.done`, and the executable suites. README and tests/CONTRACT.md updated. No work remains in flight; no deployment performed.
'"'''
p.write_text(s)
PY
cat > FIX2_DONE.txt <<'EOF'
ABYSS RACER — FIX2 COMPLETE
2026-09-12

All four requested changes implemented. All nine regression suites pass.
The 60 fps target was not achieved on this software-only server; the target
2019 MacBook Pro is unavailable and its frame rate remains unverified.

CHANGES
1. Grounded side-by-side rovers ghost when centre offset is below 0.6 rover
height; this persists until horizontal separation exceeds 1.2 rover lengths.
The rear rover draws at 55% while overlapping, with separated player tags.
Landings, roof contacts, and dome crushes remain physical. The exact requested
15 px / 380-versus-200 px/s test achieved a 302.8 px lead within 2 seconds.
Catch-up adds 25% speed and 15% torque at 60 m, fading to zero by 20 m;
grounded slipstream adds 10% speed within 8–40 m, with its HUD tag.

2. Unshielded torpedoes set crashed='Torpedoed"'!'"', count one crash and item
landed, and start the normal 2.5-second respawn. A bubble burst, flash and
shake appear in both viewports, with a distinct torpedoHit synth cue. Shield
and actual keyboard ballast-jump dodge pass. Speed is 959 px/s, 10% above
the fastest level-5 base speed (871); maximum life remains 12 seconds.
Temporary Turbo Current can buy time, but lasts only 3 seconds.

3. Race and Pearl Rush empty oxygen cause a 4-second blackout at the same
position, followed by 60% oxygen and spawn protection. No elimination.
Blackouts are separate results statistics. Last Sub Standing starts with
three lives, shown as tank icons; empty oxygen costs a life, the final loss
eliminates, and simultaneous final losses compare distance. Setup text is
updated. Crash oxygen penalties and siphon depletion trigger blackouts;
an oxygen pickup on the depletion step rescues the rover without a crash.

4. Removed adaptive downscaling and the versus 1.5x cap. Crisp (default)
uses max(1,min(devicePixelRatio,2)) in solo and versus. Manual Performance
uses 1x and fewer particles. settings.graphics persists via Title → How to
play and versus setup; legacy/invalid values default to Crisp. Full seabed
fill/sand-edge and background decoration tiles cache by terrain, chunk,
and quarter-zoom bucket. Foreground art remains individually cached so it
can clear the rover. Wheels, chassis, pickups, labels and gradients cache
as immutable ImageBitmaps, with canvas fallback and bounded resource
release. Each viewport culls independently; particles are capped; there is
no shadowBlur; unchanged HUD text is not rewritten.

Debug-only hooks: setOxygen(i,value), placePlayer(i,{x,y,vx,...}),
fireTorpedo(i), giveItem(i,id), crashPlayer(i), advance(seconds).
Indices are 0/P1 and 1/P2. AR.inspect includes blackouts, lives, ghosting,
slipstream, respawnKind, torpedo speed and explosion state.

PERFORMANCE: 1440×900 CSS VIEWPORT, deviceScaleFactor 2
Host: 4-core ARM Neoverse-N1 Linux server; Chromium headless shell 1243,
--disable-gpu. Baseline renderer: git 97fcb38. Browser runs were serial.
The committed tests/render-benchmark.cjs workload runs both production
cameras/HUDs along the same scripted trajectory, warms for 3 seconds,
then measures approximately 8 seconds of actual rAF timestamps.
Debug simulation steps are never counted as rendered frames.

Renderer                    Backing       Frames / seconds    Rendered fps
Old adaptive                1296×810       91 / 7.9997         11.38
Old forced to 2x            2880×1800       34 / 7.8497          4.33
Final Crisp 2x              2880×1800       59 / 8.0164          7.36
Final manual Performance    1440×900       207 / 8.0164        25.82

Equal-resolution improvement: 7.3599 / 4.3314 - 1 = 69.9%.
The legacy adaptive run had dropped to 0.9x by sample end and is not an
equal-quality comparison. At 2x, p95 frame duration fell from 233.4 to
150.0 ms. Immutable cache snapshots reduced the first optimization's
97.6 ms frame submission to 43.4 ms; decorations (27.4 ms), ground (6.4 ms)
and rover drawing (8.9 ms) still dominate the software path. The old
renderer deferred more raster work (2.1 ms submission despite 4.33 fps),
so submission time alone is not a before/after FPS measure.

Raw files under /tmp/abyss-fix2-fps-:
  before-adaptive.json, before-crisp.json, after-bitmap.json,
  after-performance.json.

FINAL VALIDATION — ALL PASS
- node docs/selftest.js: 27/27 physics checks
- node tests/progression.test.js: 13/13 progression/audio checks
- node tests/contacts.test.cjs: 9/9, including all 25 vehicle pairings
- node tests/versus-logic.test.cjs: 19/19
- node tests/versus-save-audio.test.cjs: save isolation and audio
- node tests/versus.test.cjs: final full Chromium suite; 20 seconds of
  simultaneous keyboard driving; all items/modes, lethal torpedo, real
  ballast dodge, respawns, lives/results, pause, save isolation and tally
- node tests/graphics.test.cjs: fixed backing sizes, graphics persistence,
  DPR floor/cap, 600 slow samples in each mode without switching, fewer
  Performance particles, live 55% overlap alpha and visual effect captures
- node tests/browser.test.cjs: unchanged solo desktop/mobile suite
